You usually don’t “rewrite to .htaccess” in PHP. `.htaccess` is an Apache config file, not a PHP file, so PHP can’t reliably edit it unless the web server allows file writes.

If you want to create or modify it from PHP, use `file_put_contents()`:

```php
$htaccess = "RewriteEngine On\n";
$htaccess .= "RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-f\n";
$htaccess .= "RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d\n";
$htaccess .= "RewriteRule .* index.php/$0 [PT,L]\n";

file_put_contents(__DIR__ . '/.htaccess', $htaccess);
```

Make sure:
- Apache `mod_rewrite` is enabled
- `AllowOverride All` is set
- the file permissions allow PHP to write

